; Regression: a deref RECEIVER on a pointer to a struct this root never lays
; out must pass the struct's ADDRESS, not a load of its first 8 bytes
; (2026-08-04).
;
; map_type answers an opaque `ptr` for any name the root has no layout for —
; the runtime-opaque set (Page, PageList, ...) and every by-value struct from
; another package. The deref arm read the LLVM type KIND back, could not tell
; that placeholder from a real pointer, and emitted a LOAD: `(*p).method()`
; then called the method with `this` = the struct's first field.
;
; Both faces were measured. Here, `(*page).get_capacity(8)` answered
; 18446181176276686314 instead of 3976, because get_capacity measures the page
; bounds from `this` as an address. Across a package boundary it was worse and
; silent: `(*t).bucket_count()` on a `pointer[Table]` returned by a
; cross-package static ran with `this` = 7 (Table's first field), and the whole
; program produced no output at all with exit code 0.
;
; The fix answers the pointer itself — NOT a copy. Copying is what the
; laid-out-struct arm does, and it is wrong for these types twice over: a
; placeholder has no size to copy, and a method that treats `this` as an
; address needs the original one.
use scaly.memory.Page
use scaly.containers.String

; A String anchors a real region page. Page.get answers a ref[Page] (since
; 2026-09-05); the shape pinned here is the DEREF RECEIVER on a POINTER to an
; opaque struct, so the pointer is taken back explicitly (a cast keeps the
; address meaning).
let anchor String(64 as size_t)
let page Page.get(anchor.c_data()) as pointer[Page]

let direct page.get_capacity(8 as size_t)
let through (*page).get_capacity(8 as size_t)

; The capacity of a page can never exceed the page size.
if direct = 0: print "FAIL direct capacity is zero"
if direct > (4096 as size_t): print "FAIL direct capacity exceeds a page"
if through <> direct: print "FAIL deref receiver disagrees with the direct call"
if direct > 0
{
    if direct <= (4096 as size_t)
    {
        if through = direct: print "PASS"
    }
}
